   "top": {
    "- 深受市民喜爱的首尔市代表品牌“气候同行卡”自9月1日起以气候同行通票的形式焕新上线，并增加交通福利- 9月在主要地铁站运营现场宣传展位，为数字弱势群体使用气候同行通票提供支持并开展换卡活动- 提前更换为全民卡，便可自9月1日起自动适用气候同行通票优惠，无需办理其他手续首尔市宣布，全民卡（气候同行通票）即将于9月1日全面上线，该卡在原全民卡所提供的乘坐公共交通工具返现优惠的基础上增加了首尔市气候同行卡的特色服务——放宽青年折扣年龄标准（19周岁-39周岁）。为配合这一计划，首尔市将加强提前换卡宣传。首尔市正引导市民提前更换卡片，以确保原气候同行卡用户可以不间断地享受交通费补贴。同时，为了尽可能减少政策变更对市民造成的不便，顺利过渡至气候同行通票，首尔市线上线下双管齐下，正在通过各种渠道集中推进说明和宣传。特别值得一提的是，在气候同行通票实体卡上线期间（中秋节前的9月1日至9月23日），首尔市将在首尔市内客流量较大的12个主要地铁站设置现场宣传展位。宣传展位的主要职责是提供换卡说明、帮助弱势群体及回收旧卡。其中，换卡说明是指为原气候同行卡用户提供换卡说明，引导原用户更换卡片；帮助弱势群体是指帮助老年人等数字弱势群体安装气候同行通票应用程序并注册K-Pass应用程序，以便他们顺利使用新卡；回收旧卡是指回收原气候同行卡实体卡及提供奖励。【江北地区】 ① 首尔站 ② 圣水 ③ 建国大学 ④ 市厅 ⑤ 延新川 ⑥ 芦原 ⑦ 弘益大学【江南地区】 ⑧ 蚕室 ⑨ 舍堂 ⑩ 宣陵 ⑪ 汝矣岛 ⑫ 加山数码园区12个现场宣传展位将面向原气候同行卡用户开展气候同行通票现场换卡活动。退还已到期的原气候同行卡，即可当场领取新上线的气候同行通票实体卡，一张旧卡免费换一张新卡。另一项活动是针对提前更换全民卡的原气候同行卡用户。此类用户可以将用完的气候同行卡携带至线下宣传展位退卡，领取咖啡优惠券或便利店优惠券。※ 气候同行卡实体卡（3000韩元） → 气候同行通票（4000韩元）关于回收后的气候同行卡实体卡，目前正在从多角度全面探讨环保应用方案，例如将旧卡用作未来仍可持续使用的气候同行卡短期券等。气候同行通票常见问题，涵盖所有须知信息Q1.气候同行卡明明用得好好的，为什么要改变政策？2024年1月，首尔市在韩国范围内率先推出可不限次数乘坐公共交通工具的定期券——气候同行卡。2026年1月，中央政府在原来的定率型返现方式的基础上结合气候同行卡不限次数乘车定期券的概念和内容，推出了全民卡。首尔市借此机会， 整合韩国全境公共交通工具、提高返现优惠、结合首尔市特色服务，进一步加强优惠力度，推动政策统一。Q2.气候同行卡可以使用到什么时候？预付费气候同行卡30日券的充值截止日期为8月31日，充值金额可在9月29日前使用。无需单独充值的后付费气候同行卡的使用截止日期为9月30日，可享受公共交通费折扣。自10月1日起，后付费气候同行卡将全面变更为不提供公共交通费折扣的普通交通卡。※ 自10月1日起，后付费气候同行卡将变更为仅限在首尔市、金浦市、高阳市、果川市、九里市、城南市、河南市和南杨州市等现有使用范围内使用的普通交通卡。但是，气候同行卡短期券（1日券、2日券、3日券、5日券、7日券）可持续使用。Q3.气候同行卡、全民卡、K-Pass、气候同行通票……太复杂了。气候同行卡是由首尔市推进开发的定期券，可以在首尔市内不限次数乘坐公共交通工具。全民卡（K-Pass）是由中央政府推进的公共交通费补贴项目，在韩国全境乘坐公共交通工具时均可享受公共交通费折扣。气候同行通票在中央政府项目“全民卡（可乘坐韩国全域公共交通）”的基础上增加了气候同行卡的特色服务（放宽青年折扣年龄标准等）。该政策旨在进一步加强首尔市民的优惠福利。在气候同行通票上线前已经在使用全民卡、K-Pass等服务的首尔市民，自9月1日起将自动适用气候同行通票优惠。Q4.使用气候同行卡时，仅需62000韩元即可不限次数乘坐公共交通工具，变成全民卡或气候同行通票后，优惠力度是不是小了？使用全民卡时，如果实际乘车金额未达到62000韩元，则返还20%；如果达到62000韩元以上，则全额返还差额。除了首尔市公共交通工具外，还可以乘坐韩国全境的公共交通工具，适用范围扩大，优惠力度也进一步提高。※ 青年、低收入群体、育有多名子女者适用的返现优惠率可达到30%至53.3%。分类普通成年人青年、老年人、育有2名子女者育有3名子女者低收入群体全民卡（气候同行通票）返现型20%30%50%53.3%定额型普通62000550004500045000Plus100000900008000080000※ 以月度公共交通费为准，在定率型、定额型普通卡和定额型Plus卡中，适用优惠力度最大的方式，于次月返现。Q5.听说截至9月使用全民卡可以享受半价折扣？4月至9月期间使用全民卡的用户可以享受额外的交通费折扣优惠。如果在上下班错峰时段使用，可以享受基本折扣；同时，当前正在实施应对高油价的半价折扣措施，以定额型普通卡为基准，每月交通费仅按30000韩元计算。※ 青年、育有2名子女者、老年人按25000韩元计算，育有3名子女者和低收入群体按22000韩元计算。Q6.听说9月1日将推出气候同行通票，必须在9月1日以后换卡吗？不是的。已经申办并使用全民卡和K-Pass卡的首尔市民自9月1日起将自动适用气候同行通票优惠。因此，在气候同行通票上线前，申办并使用全民卡（K-Pass）即可。此外，截至9月使用全民卡（K-Pass）可以享受应对高油价的半价折扣，定额型普通卡最高可享约3万韩元的额外交通费折扣。因此建议尽快换卡。Q7.35周岁至39周岁的青年更换全民卡后，是不是不能再继续享受折扣优惠了？自9月1日起，35周岁至39周岁的青年同样适用实际乘车金额未达到55000韩元时返还30%的优惠；达到55000韩元以上时，享受定额计费及返现等优惠。* Plus卡为90000韩元。截至9月实施全民卡半价折扣政策，最高可享约3万韩元公共交通费折扣。Q8.什么时候适用退伍军人（至42周岁）青年折扣、首尔自行车叮铃铃联动折扣、文化设施联动折扣？退伍军人青年折扣和首尔自行车叮铃铃联动折扣等特色服务需要与有关机构协商并优化系统；而文化设施联动折扣则需要修订条例。首尔市将加快推进相关进程，计划于2026年年内实施。Q9.如何申办并使用全民卡和气候同行通票？通过发卡机构申办信用卡或借记卡形式的全民卡（K-Pass），领卡后访问K-Pass网站（https://korea-pass.kr/）注册该卡并使用，即可从次月起享受返现优惠。在便利店等地购买的预付费全民卡，必须在购卡后前往发卡机构（T-money、EZL等）的网站或应用程序注册卡号和返现账户。在K-Pass网站注册卡片后使用，即可享受返现优惠。通过手机应用程序申办的预付费全民卡也需要在发卡机构网站或应用程序上注册后前往K-Pass网站注册。但是，9月1日前已经使用全民卡的首尔市民无需另行换卡，9月1日起自动适用气候同行通票优惠。Q10.全民卡和气候同行通票是必须从每月1日起开始使用吗？不是的。全民卡（气候同行通票）虽然是以每月月底产生的实际公共交通费为准适用折扣优惠，但是可以随时访问K-Pass网站等注册卡片并使用，届时会以当月使用的金额为准适用返现优惠。申办或购买全民卡等卡片后，使用前必须访问K-Pass网站登记个人信息和卡号，才能享受公共交通费返现优惠。Q11.原气候同行卡实体卡是花3000韩元买的，购卡费可以退回吗？自9月起的约一个月期间，将在首尔市的12个主要地铁站 （首尔站、蚕室、舍堂、宣陵、汝矣岛、圣水、加山数码园区、建国大学、市厅、延新川、芦原、弘益大学）开展换卡活动。市民退还使用完的原气候同行卡，可以免费更换新上线的气候同行通票实体卡，已经换卡的市民可领取咖啡优惠券或便利店优惠券。Q12.气候同行卡可以在金浦、高阳、果川、九里、城南、河南、南杨州等地使用，气候同行通票也可以吗？不可以。全民卡（气候同行通票）以居住地为准提供公共交通费返现优惠，适用对象仅限首尔市民。金浦、高阳、果川、九里、城南、河南和南杨州等地的市民需要更换为所在地区的全民卡服务“京畿通票”。Q13.可持续使用的气候同行卡短期券的使用地区有哪些？今后短期券的使用范围限定为首尔地区，但可在仁川国际机场下车，此前适用的金浦、高阳、果川、九里、城南、河南和南杨州等地区不再属于可使用地区。Q14.气候同行卡3万韩元返现政策的申请截止日期是什么时候？4月至6月，为了应对高油价，面向气候同行卡30日券完成充值并使用期满的用户提供的3万韩元返现优惠，可在8月31日前通过T-money Card  Pay网站 （https://pay.tmoney.co.kr/indexReal.dev）申请。Q15.上网不便的老年人或外国人如何申请返现优惠？不方便进行线上申请的65岁以上老年人、迁居至其他地区的人员、外国人、归化及居民登记号码变更的人员、无法进行快捷身份验证的人员（例如未满14周岁者、2G手机用户等）可通过邮寄、传真、电子邮件等人工手动申请3万韩元返现。申请表可通过T-money Card  Pay网站弹窗下载打印，只需填写姓名、卡号、账户号码并提交可确认居住地的居民登记证明简本（若是外国人，则提交外国人事实证明）等材料，经人工审核后即可获得返现。※ 邮寄申请：（04535）首尔特别市中区小公路70，首尔中央邮局邮政信箱2023号，T-money股份有限公司气候同行卡人工退款申请负责人（收）※ 电子邮箱：***@**.**/传真：02-6989-0120*Q16.外国人也可以使用K-Pass吗？仅限有外国人登录证号码的外国人注册会员。※ 注册会员时，在居民登录证号码一栏输入外国人登录证号码即可注册。※ 如果无法通过外国人登录证号码确认居住事实，可在完成注册后，使用居住事实确认书验证居住地。● 注册后验证居住地的方法 ●1.访问K-Pass网站或应用程序并注册会员。2.使用ID和密码登录。3.前往“MY  我的地方自治团体”菜单。4.点击“上传文件”按钮。5.上传韩国居住事实确认书（外国人）。※来源： https://korea-pass.kr/": 1,
    "- Climate Card, a beloved signature brand of the Seoul Metropolitan Government, will expand transportation benefits as Climate Pass starting September 1- Promotional booths will operate at major subway stations throughout September to assist users with Climate Pass, including support for users who may have difficulty accessing digital services, as well as card exchange events- Users who switch to Everyone’s Card in advance will automatically receive Climate Pass benefits starting September 1, with no additional steps requiredThe Seoul Metropolitan Government (SMG) announced that it will step up advance outreach for Everyone’s Card (Climate Pass), scheduled to launch on September 1, 2026. The new pass combines the nationwide public transportation fare refund benefits provided by Everyone’s Card with special benefits offered through Seoul’s Climate Card, including expanding the age range for the youth discount to 19–39.Accordingly, SMG is encouraging existing Climate Card users to switch to Climate Pass in advance so that they do not experience any interruption in their transportation fare benefits. To ensure a smooth transition to Climate Pass and minimize any inconvenience caused by the policy change, the city is conducting intensive information campaigns and promotional activities through a variety of online and offline channels.In particular, promotional booths will be set up at 12 major subway stations with high passenger traffic in Seoul from September 1, when the physical Climate Pass card launches, through September 23, ahead of Chuseok. At the promotional booths, Seoul will provide guidance and assistance with the transition, including information for existing Climate Card users on switching their cards; support for users who may have difficulty accessing digital services, including older adults, with app installation and K-Pass app registration needed to use Climate Pass; and the collection of existing physical Climate Cards, along with a card exchange event.Subway Stations in Gangbuk:① Seoul Station② Seongsu③ Konkuk University④ City Hall⑤ Yeonsinnae⑥ Nowon⑦ Hongik UniversitySubway Stations in Gangnam:⑧ Jamsil⑨ Sadang⑩ Seolleung⑪ Yeouido⑪ Gasan Digital ComplexAt the 12 promotional booths, an on-site Climate Pass card exchange event will be held for existing Climate Card users. Users who return an expired Climate Card can exchange it on a one-for-one basis at no additional cost for the newly launched physical Climate Pass card.In addition, existing Climate Card users who have switched to Everyone’s Card in advance can return their used Climate Cards at the promotional booths and exchange them for a coffee or convenience store coupon. *Physical Climate Card (KRW 3,000) → Climate Pass (KRW 4,000)SMG is also exploring various environmentally friendly ways to reuse the collected physical Climate Cards, including repurposing them as short-term Climate Cards, which will remain available.Climate Pass QA: Everything You Need to KnowQ1. I was happy with my Climate Card. Why is the policy changing?Seoul launched the Climate Card in January 2024 as Korea’s first unlimited public transportation pass. Then, in January 2026, the national government introduced Everyone’s Card, incorporating the concept and benefits of Climate Card’s unlimited user model into its existing percentage-based fare refund system. The new policy brings together nationwide public transportation coverage, enhanced fare refunds, and Seoul’s specialized benefits, while consolidating the two programs into one.Q2. How long can I use my Climate Card?If you have a prepaid 30-day Climate Card, you can recharge it through August 31. Any pass recharged by then can be used through September 29, the final day of its validity period. If you have a postpaid Climate Card, which does not require recharging, you can continue using it through September 30 and receive public transportation fare benefits. Starting October 1, postpaid Climate Cards will be converted into regular transportation cards without public transportation fare benefits.*Starting October 1, postpaid Climate Cards will be converted into regular transportation cards that can only be used within the current service area, including Seoul and the cites of Gimpo, Goyang, Gwacheon, Guri, Seongnam, Hanam, and Namyangju. However, Climate Card short-term passes (1-, 2-, 3-, 5-, and 7-day passes) will continue to be available.Q3. Climate Card, Everyone’s Card, K-Pass, Climate Pass… It’s all so confusing!We get it—there are a lot of names to keep track of. Climate Card is a pass operated by SMG that provides unlimited public transportation access in Seoul. Everyone’s Card (K-Pass) is a national government program that provides public transportation fare support, including discounts on public transportation fare nationwide.Climate Pass combines Everyone’s Card, which provides nationwide public transportation fare support, with Climate Card’s specialized benefits, such as the expanded age eligibility for the youth discount. It is designed to provide enhanced benefits specifically for Seoul residents. If you’re a Seoul resident already using Everyone’s Card, K-Pass, or another eligible service before Climate Pass launches, the Climate Pass benefits will automatically apply to you starting September 1.Q4. I could use unlimited public transportation for KRW 62,000 with Climate Card. Won’t I get fewer benefits if I switch to Everyone’s Card or Climate Pass?Under Everyone’s Card, users receive a 20% refund when their transportation spending is less than KRW 62,000, or a full refund of the difference when their spending is KRW 62,000 or more. The program also allows users to take public transportation nationwide, rather than only in Seoul, expanding both coverage and benefits.*Youth, low-income individuals, and households with multiple children are eligible for refunds ranging from 30% to 53.3%.TypeGeneralYouth, Older Adults, Two-Child HouseholdsThree-Child (or More) HouseholdsLow-IncomeEveryone’s Card(Climate Pass)Percentage-Based Refund20%30%50%53.3%Flat-Rate RefundGeneral62,00055,00045,00045,000Plus100,00090,00080,00080,000*Based on monthly public transportation expenses, the least expensive option among the percentage-based refund, standard flat-rate, and plus flat-rate options will be applied, with the refund issued the following month.Q5. I heard there’s a half-price discount if I use Everyone’s Card through September. Is that true?If you use Everyone’s Card from April through September, you can receive additional public transportation fare savings. A temporary half-price fare measure introduced in response to high fuel prices is currently in effect, providing additional fare savings during off-peak hours and reducing the monthly fare under the standard flat-rate plan to KRW 30,000. *The monthly fare is KRW 25,000 for youth, older adults, and households with two children, and KRW 22,000 for households with three or more children and low-income users.Q6. Climate Pass launches on September 1. Do I need to switch after September 1?No. Seoul residents who are already using an existing Everyone’s Card or K-Pass card will automatically receive Climate Pass benefits starting September 1, so there’s no need to wait until Climate Pass officially launches to start using Everyone’s Card (K-Pass).Also, if you use Everyone’s Card (K-Pass) through September, the temporary half-price fare measure introduced in response to high fuel prices will apply. Under the standard flat-rate plan, you can receive up to approximately KRW 30,000 in additional transportation fare savings, so switching sooner means you can start receiving the benefits sooner.Q7. I’m 35–39 years old. Won’t I lose my benefits if I switch to Everyone’s Card?No. Starting September 1, users ages 35–39 will also be eligible for a 30% refund if they spend less than KRW 55,000, while those who spend KRW 55,000 or more will receive the flat-rate benefit and refund, among other benefits. (*The Plus plan costs KRW 90,000.)Through September, the temporary half-price fare measure for Everyone’s Card will also provide up to approximately KRW 30,000 in public transportation fare savings.Q8. When will benefits such as the youth discount for discharged military personnel (up to age 42), the Ttareungi public bike-linked discount, and cultural facility discounts take effect?Specialized services such as the youth discount for discharged military personnel and the Ttareungi public bike-linked discount require consultation with relevant agencies and system upgrades. Discounts linked to cultural facilities require an amendment to the relevant ordinance. SMG plans to implement these benefits within the year by expediting the necessary administrative procedures.Q9. How do I get and use Everyone’s Card and Climate Pass?If you get an Everyone’s Card (K-Pass) in the form of a credit or debit card through a card company, register the card on the K-Pass website (https://korea-pass.kr/) after receiving it and then start using it. You can then receive the refund starting the following month.For prepaid Everyone’s Cards purchased at convenience stores and other locations, you need to register your card number and refund account information through the card issuer’s website or app (such as Tmoney or EZL), and then register the card on the K-Pass website before using it to receive refund benefits.Prepaid Everyone’s Cards issued through a mobile app must also be registered through the issuer’s website or app and then on the K-Pass website. However, Seoul residents who are already using Everyone’s Card before September 1 will automatically receive Climate Pass benefits starting September 1 without having to switch cards separately.Q10. Do I have to start using Everyone’s Card or Climate Pass on the first day of every month?No. Everyone’s Card (Climate Pass) calculates fare benefits based on your public transportation expenses incurred at the end of each month. However, if you register your card on the K-Pass website or other relevant platform and start using it at any time during the month, you can receive refund benefits based on your transportation spending for that month.To receive public transportation fare support, you must register your personal information and card number on the K-Pass website after obtaining or purchasing an Everyone’s Card and then use the registered card for public transportation.Q11. I bought and used a physical Climate Card for KRW 3,000. Can I get a refund?Starting in September, Seoul will hold a card exchange event for approximately one month at 12 major subway stations in Seoul: Seoul Station, Jamsil, Sadang, Seolleung, Yeouido, Seongsu, Gasan Digital Complex, Konkuk University, City Hall, Yeonsinnae, Nowon, and Hongik University. If you return your used Climate Card, you can exchange it at no additional cost for a newly launched Climate Pass card. For users who have already switched to Climate Pass, Seoul will also hold an event where they can exchange their used Climate Cards for a coffee or convenience store coupon.Q12. I was able to use Climate Card in Gimpo, Goyang, Gwacheon, Guri, Seongnam, Hanam, and Namyangju. Can I use Climate Pass there as well?No. Everyone’s Card (Climate Pass) is a public transportation fare refund program based on the user’s place of residence, so it is available only to Seoul residents. Residents of Gimpo, Goyang, Gwacheon, Guri, Seongnam, Hanam, and Namyangju will need to switch to The Gyeonggi Pass, the Everyone’s Card program available to residents of those areas.Q13. What areas will the Climate Card short-term passes, which will continue to be offered, cover?Going forward, the short-term passes will be valid for travel within Seoul and for trips ending at Incheon International Airport. The existing service areas of Gimpo, Goyang, Gwacheon, Guri, Seongnam, Hanam, and Namyangju will no longer be included.Q14. When is the deadline to apply for the KRW 30,000 Climate Card cashback?Users who recharged and used a 30-day Climate Card pass between April and June under the high fuel price relief measures can apply for the KRW 30,000 cashbacks through August 31 via the Tmoney Card  Pay website (https://pay.tmoney.co.kr/indexReal.dev).Q15. How can older adults or foreigners who have difficulty using the Internet apply for the cashback?For those who have difficulty applying online, a manual application for the KRW 30,000 cashback is also available by mail, fax, or email. This includes adults aged 65 and over, people who have changed their place of residence, foreigners, people who have naturalized or changed their resident registration number, and those without an easy way to verify their identity (such as children under 14 and users of 2G mobile phones).The application form can be downloaded from a pop-up on the Tmoney Card  Pay website. Applicants can submit the completed form along with their name, card number, bank account number, and a resident registration abstract verifying their address (or, for foreign nationals, a certificate of foreign resident registration). The application will be manually reviewed before the cashback is issued.*Mailing Address: (04535) Climate Card Manual Refund Application Manager, Tmoney Co., Ltd., Seoul Central Post Office P.O. Box 2023, 70 Sogong-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul*Email: ***@**.**/ Fax: +82-2-6989-0120Q16. Can foreigners use K-Pass?Only foreigners with a Foreign Resident Registration Number can sign up.*When signing up, you can enter your Foreign Resident Registration Number instead of a Resident Registration Number.*If your place of residence cannot be verified using your Foreign Resident Registration Number, you can verify your address with a Certificate of Residence Verification after completing registration.● How to Verify Place of Residence After Signing Up ●1. Sign up on the K-Pass website or app.2. Log in with your ID and password.3. Go to [MY]  [My Local Government].4. Click [Upload File].5. Upload your Certificate of Domestic Residence (for Foreigners).*Source: https://korea-pass.kr/": 1,
    "[首尔市] 儿童眼部健康守护者“眼镜折扣”项目指南■ 申请日期：8月25日（周二）09:00~8月31日（周一）18:00■ 申请方法：在线申请- 首尔市公共服务预约系统（https://yeyak.seoul.go.kr/）→ 文化体验 → 文化活动* 使用家长名下的账号登录后申请（预约时输入子女出生日期）。■ 折扣内容- 支持项目：通过政企合作提供眼镜优惠券（仅限儿童镜片和镜框）- 折扣率：非活动商品：10%~20%，活动商品：在原售价基础上提供5%折扣■ 合作企业- 首尔市眼镜协会、第一50眼镜、DAVICH眼镜、STAR VISION（OLENS）、OPTIC LIFE■ 注意事项- 6周岁及以下儿童配镜时，需提供眼科医生处方。- 每名儿童可享受1套镜片加镜框折扣。": 1,
    "[Seoul Metropolitan Government] “Protecting Children’s Eye Health” Eyeglass Discount Support Program• Application Period: Tuesday, August 25, 9:00 AM – Monday, August 31, 6:00 PM• How to Apply: Online- Seoul Public Service Reservation System (https://yeyak.seoul.go.kr/) → Cultural Experiences → Cultural Events* Log in with a parent’s account and apply (Enter the child’s date of birth when making a reservation.)• Support Details- Items Covered: Eyeglass discount coupons provided through public-private partnerships (Children’s eyeglass lenses and frames only)- Discount Rate: 10–20% off non-promotional items; 5% off the regular selling price of promotional items• Partner Companies- Seoul Opticians Association, Top 50 Glasses, Davich Optical, Starvision (O-LENS), Optic Life• Important Notes- Ophthalmologist’s prescription required for eyeglasses for children aged 6 or younger- Discount on one set of children’s eyeglass lenses and frames": 1,
    "<img src=\"https://global.seoul.go.kr/contents/commoneditor/20******08da731-f781-45b1-8186-fe66c91200de.jpg\" alt=\"어린이 행복 프로젝트 어린이 눈건강 지킴이 안경 할인 지원\r\n신청대상 서울시 거주 초등학생 이하 자녀가 있는 가구\r\n지원내용\r\n안경 20% 할인쿠폰 지급\r\n* 기존 할인행사품목은 5% 할인(업체 개별 문의)\r\n* 서울시안경사회, 다비치안경, 으뜸50안경,\r\n오렌즈(스타비전), 옵틱 라이프 참여\r\n신청 및 구입 방법\r\n신청자 접수\r\n서울시 공공서비스예약\r\n(http://yeyak.seoul.go.kr/)\r\n안경 할인쿠폰 발행\r\n안경업체(본사)\r\n서울시안경사회\r\n→ 신청자\r\n안경 구입\r\n신청한 안경업체에\r\n할인쿠폰 제시 후 구입\r\n신청기간\r\n2026.8. 25.(화)~8. 31.(월) (7일간)\r\n할인쿠폰 발송\r\n2026.9.4.(금)\">[서울시] 어린이 눈건강 지킴이 안경 할인 지원 사업 안내■접수 기간 : 8.25(화) 09:00~8.31(월) 18:00■신청 방법 : 온라인 접수-서울시 공공서비스예약시스템(https://yeyak.seoul.go.kr/) → 문화체험 → 문화행사* 부모 명의 아이디 로그인 후 신청(예약 시 자녀 생년월일 입력)■지원 사항-지원 품목 : 민관협력을 통한 안경 할인쿠폰 제공(어린이 안경렌즈, 안경테만 가능)-할인율 : 비 행사품목 10~20%, 행사품목 기존 판매가격 5%■ 협약업체-서울시 안경사회,으뜸50안경, 다비치안경, 스타비젼(오렌즈), 옵틱라이프■유의사항-만 6세 이하 아동의 경우 안경 조제 시 안과의사 처방 필요-어린이 안경렌즈, 안경테 1세트 할인 가능[ソウル市]子どもの目の健康を守るメガネ割引支援事業のご案内■受付期間：8月25日（火）09:00～8月31日（月）18:00■申込方法：オンライン申込-ソウル市公共サービス予約システム（https://yeyak.seoul.go.kr/) → 文化体験 → 文化行事* 保護者名義のIDでログイン後、お申し込みください。（予約時にお子さまの生年月日を入力します。）■支援内容-対象：官民連携によるメガネ割引クーポンを提供（子ども用メガネレンズとフレームのみ対象）-割引率：キャンペーン対象外商品 10～20％、キャンペーン対象商品 通常販売価格の5％■提携業者-ソウル市眼鏡士会、ウットム50メガネ、DAVICHメガネ、スタービジョン（OLENS）、オプティックライフ■注意事項-満6歳以下のお子さまの場合、メガネの作製時には眼科医の処方箋が必要です。-子ども用メガネレンズ・フレーム1セットにつき割引が適用されます。[Thành phố Seoul] Thông báo chương trình hỗ trợ giảm giá kính mắt bảo vệ sức khỏe mắt trẻ em■ Thời gian đăng ký: 09:00 ngày 25/8 (Thứ Ba) - 18:00 ngày 31/8 (Thứ Hai)■ Cách đăng ký: Đăng ký trực tuyến- Hệ thống Đặt trước Dịch vụ Công Thành phố Seoul (https://yeyak.seoul.go.kr/) → Trải nghiệm văn hóa → Sự kiện văn hóa*Đăng nhập bằng tài khoản đứng tên phụ huynh rồi đăng ký (khi đặt trước, nhập ngày sinh của trẻ)■ Nội dung hỗ trợ- Hạng mục hỗ trợ: Cấp phiếu giảm giá kính mắt thông qua hợp tác công - tư (chỉ áp dụng cho tròng kính trẻ em và gọng kính)- Mức giảm: Sản phẩm không thuộc chương trình khuyến mãi giảm 10-20%; sản phẩm khuyến mãi giảm thêm 5% trên giá bán hiện tại■ Đơn vị liên kết- Hiệp hội Kính mắt Thành phố Seoul, Top 50 Glasses, Davich, Star Vision (O-Lens), Optic Life■ Lưu ý- Trẻ từ 6 tuổi trở xuống cần có đơn kính của bác sĩ nhãn khoa khi làm kính- Chỉ áp dụng giảm giá cho 1 bộ gồm tròng kính trẻ em và gọng kính": 1,
    "在自然低语中享受清凉夏日：首尔漫步路第9路线（大母山和九龙山）徒步之旅近日天气炎热，即使静静站着也会汗珠直冒。于是笔者离开沥青覆盖的市中心，迈步走向首尔漫步路第9路线（大母山和九龙山）。之所以选择这里，是因为好奇首尔市为何将它选为应对酷暑的首尔漫步路夏季五大推荐路线之一。☞[相关报道] 寻找清凉林荫路？ 首尔漫步路夏季五大推荐路线（韩语）首尔漫步路第9路线（大母山和九龙山）是一条从水西站延伸至梅轩市民之林、全长10.7公里（约需4小时50分钟）的步行路线。沿途土路连接着茂密森林，可尽情享受天然森林浴，树荫充足，堪称城市型林间避暑胜地。走出地铁3号线水西站6号出口，转向大母山方向，皮肤感受到的空气质感已然不同。在闷热的酷暑中疲惫不堪的身心，踏入森林不过几分钟，便瞬间平静下来。密密层层的树木如同天然遮阳伞，严严实实地挡住了炽烈的阳光，而透过树叶缝隙洒落的阳光不再是火焰，而像一幅清凉的画卷在闪烁。最令人赞叹的，是脚底触碰到松软土路时的质感。对于在冷硬的混凝土城市里每天只踩着坚硬人行道砖的双脚来说，第9路线的土路就像大自然铺就的丝绸地毯。凉凉的林风拂过，额头的汗水渐渐消退，深吸一口气，清新的芬多精香气沁入肺腑深处。“啊，这就是大自然带来的免费降温吧！”这样的念头油然而生。那是一种与人工空调风截然不同的凉意，连头脑都为之清醒的清凉。以前提到首尔漫步路，总觉得有8条路线、全长超过20公里，心里会想着“我敢挑战吗？”而不敢尝试。但经过此次首尔漫步路2.0改版，细分为21条路线，平均耗时缩短至3小时左右，负担大大减轻。距离和时间缩短后，不再有必须走完的压力，反而能全身心欣赏路旁绽放的野花、倾听随风飘落的树叶声响，享受真正的疗愈徒步。途中偶遇印章邮筒，用手机二维码打卡认证时，总会涌起一种奇妙的成就感，仿佛在记录独属于自己的健康夏日。路上遇到的其他市民，脸上也少有疲倦，更多的是绿意盈盈的闲适。同时，首尔市提醒，为安全利用夏季漫步路，建议避开酷热的中午时段，选择相对凉爽的上午或傍晚前往，并务必携带足量饮用水以防脱水。此外，登山前应确认高温预警等气象特报，若发布相关预警，应避免强行进行户外活动和登山。这一天，滴滴汗水仿佛洗净体内应排出的废物与压力，成为净化之水。在森林赐予的凉爽树荫下，我充满了能战胜今夏的最健康、最美好的能量，满载而归。如果你在疲惫的都市生活中渴望如同沙漠绿洲般清凉的慰藉，我强烈推荐各位毫不犹豫地踏上这条林间路。\r\n首尔漫步路第9路线（大母山和九龙山）路线：水西站 – 大母山山腰 – 佛国寺 – 九龙山 – 如意川 – 梅轩市民之林，全程10.7公里（步行约需4小时50分钟）交通：地铁3号线水西站6号出口；新盆唐线良才市民之林站（梅轩市民之林）难度：中级（含部分山路和上下坡）查看更多首尔漫步路信息：https://chinese.seoul.go.kr/服务/文化休闲/首尔漫步路/漫步路介绍/\r\n\r\n\r\n": 1,
    "ool Summer Days, Guided by Nature: Trekking Seoul Trail Route 9 (Daemosan and Guryongsan Mountains)These days, you can break a sweat just by standing still. So I decided to leave the asphalt-covered city behind and head to Seoul Trail Route 9: Daemosan and Guryongsan Mountains. I wanted to see for myself why Seoul had chosen this trail as one of its five recommended summer Seoul Trail routes.☞[Related Article] Five Recommended Summer Routes on the Seoul Trail (Korean)Seoul Trail Route 9, which runs along the slopes of Daemosan and Guryongsan Mountains, is a 10.7-kilometer trail from Suseo Station to Maeheon Citizen’s Forest, taking about 4 hours and 50 minutes to complete on foot. With forested dirt paths winding through dense woodland, the trail is perfect for a refreshing walk in nature. Thanks to the ample shade provided by the trees, it offers an ideal forest escape right in the heart of the city.As soon as I left Exit 6 of Suseo Station on Subway Line 3 and headed toward Daemosan Mountain, I could feel a noticeable change in the air. Worn out by the sweltering heat, I felt my body and mind relax within minutes of stepping into the forest. The dense canopy formed a natural umbrella, shielding me from the scorching sun, while sunlight filtering through the leaves created a cool, refreshing atmosphere rather than adding to the heat.What impressed me most was the soft, earthy trail beneath my feet. After spending my days walking on hard pavement in the concrete jungle, the soft dirt path on Route 9 felt like a silk carpet laid out by nature. A cool breeze swept through the forest, easing the sweat on my forehead. As soon as I took a deep breath and savored the fresh scent of phytoncides, I thought, “Ah, so this is nature’s own free air conditioning!” It was a refreshing kind of cool, completely different from the artificial chill of an air conditioner—one that seemed to clear my head as well.I used to think of the Seoul Trail as a daunting trek spanning eight routes and more than 20 kilometers, and I remember wondering, “Could I really do this?” But following the Seoul Trail 2.0 revamp, the trail has been divided into 21 shorter routes, bringing the average walking time down to around three hours and making each route much more manageable. With shorter distances and walking times, I no longer felt pressured to complete a long trek. Instead, I could slow down and enjoy the journey—stopping to admire a wildflower along the way or listen to leaves rustling in the breeze. It felt like the perfect way to recharge in nature.Along the way, I came across mailbox-style stamp stations where hikers can check in by scanning a mobile QR code. Each one gave me a sense of accomplishment, as if I were keeping a record of a healthy summer. The other hikers I encountered also looked more refreshed than weary, energized by the surrounding greenery.For safe summer hiking, the Seoul Metropolitan Government (SMG) recommends avoiding the hottest part of the day and hiking during the cooler morning hours or around sunset. Hikers are also advised to bring plenty of water to stay hydrated. Before setting out, check for weather alerts, including heat wave warnings, and avoid strenuous outdoor activities if an alert is in effect.By the end of the day, the sweat rolling down my face felt like it was washing away the stress and fatigue I had been carrying. Under the cool shade of the forest, I headed home feeling refreshed, energized, and ready for the rest of the summer. If you need a refreshing escape from the fatigue of everyday city life—a peaceful oasis amid the urban landscape—I highly recommend taking a walk along this forest trail.\r\nSeoul Trail Route 9: Daemosan and Guryongsan Mountains- Route (10.7 km): Suseo Station → Daemosan Mountain foothills → Bulguksa Temple → Guryongsan Mountain → Yeouicheon Stream → Maeheon Citizen’s Forest (approx. 4 hr 50 min on foot)- Getting There: Exit 6 of Suseo Station on Subway Line 3 or Yangjae Citizen’s Forest Station on the Shinbundang Line (Maeheon Citizen’s Forest)- Difficulty: Intermediate (includes mountain trails and uphill and downhill sections)- Learn more about the Seoul Trail: https://english.seoul.go.kr/service/amusement/seoul-trail/01-seoul-trail/\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n": 1,
    "체류형 관광 활성화 및 글로벌 관광도시 조성을 위해 「2026년 보령 한달 살기」 사업을 추진합니다.🌍 사업개요- 모집기간: 2026. 8. 18.(화) ~ 8. 31.(월)- 선정규모: 외국인 참가자 5팀 (1~2인/팀), 내국인 참가자 10팀 (1~2인/팀)- 여행기간: 2026. 9. 18.(금) ~ 11. 30.(월) 중 7일 ~ 30일 자율 선택- 참여대상: 공고일 기준 충청남도 외 지역에 주소지를 둔 만 19세 이상 누구나- 세부사항: 붙임 참고- 주요내용: 보령에 장기간 머물며 자유여행 진행- 여행범위: 체류(숙박) 및 과제수행은 보령에서 진행, 충청남도 타 시·군 방문 가능, 단, 지원비의 50% 이상은 보령에서 집행📝 신청 개요- 신청기간: 2026. 8. 18.(화) ~ 8. 31.(월)※ 예산 범위 내, 포기자 발생 시 예비순위자 순차 선정- 신청방법: 이메일 접수 → ***@**.**문의처: 보령시 관광과 관광마케팅팀 ☎ ***- 선정기준: 총점 70점 미만 시 선정 제외": 1,
